@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `baominh-par-claim`
IMPORT `baominh-par-fixtures`

-- THE HOSTILE READING: evidence for the findings in NOTES.md section 4. Each #ASSERT here states
-- what the document, encoded as written, actually answers in a scenario where a reader would
-- expect something else. They pass: that is the point. A finding is a defect in the instrument,
-- not in the encoding; the finding's number in NOTES.md is on each block. Findings that the
-- encoding cannot demonstrate are marked "reading only" in NOTES.md and have no block here.
-- Amounts are scenario values in VND.

§ `Findings`

§§ `Finding 1: property insured elsewhere is excluded, so General Condition 6 never applies`

-- Exclusion 8(i), "các tài sản đã được thu xếp bảo hiểm theo cách khác" (src:168), takes out
-- property otherwise insured; General Condition 6 (src:298-306) pays a rateable proportion of the
-- same loss. The stock is also insured elsewhere for 500,000,000.
`stock insured elsewhere too` MEANS `A damaged item` WITH
    `the item insured`                  IS `the stock`
    `kind`                              IS stock
    `the chain of causation`            IS LIST (`directly` fire)
    `circumstances`                     IS `circumstances with` (LIST `insured some other way`)
    `valuation`                         IS `The valuation of the item` WITH
        `the Damage, valued at the time of the loss`                      IS 100000000
        `the part of the Damage arising from a cause not excluded`        IS NOTHING
        `the actual value of the item at the time of the loss`            IS JUST 500000000
        `sums insured by other insurances of the same property or loss`   IS LIST 500000000
        `the amount the marine policy would pay if this policy did not exist` IS NOTHING
        `the costs of the media`                                          IS NOTHING
    `what the Insured told the Insurer` IS `nothing false was said`
    `changes under General Condition 8` IS EMPTY
    `claimed as a cost of changing or adding to a computer system, programme, software or chip` IS FALSE

-- what General Condition 6 would pay, if it were ever reached: half, 50,000,000
#ASSERT `General Condition 6 applied to` `stock insured elsewhere too` 100000000 EQUALS 50000000
-- what the document pays: nothing, by exclusion 8
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss of the item` `stock insured elsewhere too`) EQUALS `nothing is payable because` (LIST "exclusion 8", "the amount for the loss, after the conditions, the caps and the deductible, is nil")

§§ `Finding 2: one late notice, or one omitted precaution, defeats the whole claim`

-- The insuring clause makes every condition a condition precedent (src:9-11); General Condition
-- 9(a) requires notice "ngay lập tức" (src:337-340), undefined; General Condition 12 requires
-- "mọi biện pháp" (every measure) to prevent loss (src:401-402). A covered fire of 100,000,000:
GIVEN cd IS A `The Insured's conduct`
GIVETH A `A loss`
`the ordinary fire, with conduct` cd MEANS
    `a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of` (LIST (`a damaged` buildings `by` (LIST `directly` fire))) `with theft` NOTHING `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` cd `premium` `the premium paid on time`

#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`the ordinary fire, with conduct` `good conduct`) EQUALS `the Insurer must pay` 90000000
-- notice not immediate (a judgement on the facts): nothing at all, not a reduction
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`the ordinary fire, with conduct` (`conduct with` EMPTY `and` (`a claims procedure with` (JUST 10) NOTHING FALSE TRUE))) EQUALS `nothing is payable because` (LIST "General Condition 9(a)(i): no immediate measures to minimise the loss", "General Condition 9(a)(ii): no immediate written notice to the Insurer")
-- one precaution not taken, unconnected with the fire: nothing at all
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`the ordinary fire, with conduct` (`conduct with` (LIST `a precaution not taken`) `and` `the procedure followed`)) EQUALS `nothing is payable because` (LIST "General Condition 12: not every precaution to prevent loss was taken")

§§ `Finding 3: the second arbitrator can be appointed on one day only`

-- Evidence: the three #TRACE directives under General Condition 7 in
-- baominh-par-tests-conditions.l4 (month 1: a nullity; month 2: fulfilled; month 3: the other
-- party may appoint a sole arbitrator).

§§ `Finding 6: cover ceases without any link to the loss`

-- General Condition 8(b) (src:328-329): the building unattended for 30 days, then an earthquake.
`the earthquake after 30 days unattended` MEANS `A damaged item` WITH
    `the item insured`                  IS `the building`
    `kind`                              IS buildings
    `the chain of causation`            IS LIST (`directly` earthquake)
    `circumstances`                     IS `the ordinary circumstances`
    `valuation`                         IS `the ordinary valuation`
    `what the Insured told the Insurer` IS `nothing false was said`
    `changes under General Condition 8` IS LIST (`A change affecting the item` WITH `the change` IS `the building or premises left unattended` 30, `accepted by endorsement before the loss` IS FALSE)
    `claimed as a cost of changing or adding to a computer system, programme, software or chip` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss of the item` `the earthquake after 30 days unattended`) EQUALS `nothing is payable because` (LIST "General Condition 8: the policy had ceased to attach to the property after a change the Insurer had not accepted", "the amount for the loss, after the conditions, the caps and the deductible, is nil")

§§ `Finding 8: the short-period scale's rows overlap`

-- "Đến 3 tháng" ends at 3 and "Từ 3 đến 6 tháng" begins at 3; likewise at 6 (src:278-280). The
-- generated rows carry the printed numbers: each row's upper edge is the next row's lower edge.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A row of the short-period scale`
`the scale row numbered` n MEANS
    CONSIDER drop (n MINUS 1) `the short-period scale`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the short-period scale has no row for that period`
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN r

#ASSERT (`the scale row numbered` 1)'s `months, up to and including` EQUALS JUST ((`the scale row numbered` 2)'s `months, from more than`)
#ASSERT (`the scale row numbered` 2)'s `months, up to and including` EQUALS JUST ((`the scale row numbered` 3)'s `months, from more than`)

§§ `Finding 9: the two lists of perils written back do not match`

-- Exclusion 6 (src:135-139) and exclusion 11 (src:233-237) each write back a list of perils.
-- Riot ("bạo loạn") and hail ("mưa đá") are on the second and not the first, so a computer damaged
-- by them is excluded under exclusion 6.
#ASSERT `the effect of the exclusions on` (`a loss of the item` (`a damaged` computers `by` (LIST `directly` riot))) (`a damaged` computers `by` (LIST `directly` riot)) EQUALS `excluded by` (LIST "exclusion 6")
#ASSERT `the effect of the exclusions on` (`a loss of the item` (`a damaged` computers `by` (LIST `directly` hail))) (`a damaged` computers `by` (LIST `directly` hail)) EQUALS `excluded by` (LIST "exclusion 6")
-- while demonstration ("biểu tình"), which is on the first list, is written back
#ASSERT `the effect of the exclusions on` (`a loss of the item` (`a damaged` computers `by` (LIST `directly` demonstration))) (`a damaged` computers `by` (LIST `directly` demonstration)) EQUALS `no exclusion applies`

§§ `Finding 14: money confirmed as insured is not covered against burglary`

-- Exclusion 6(a) (src:127-130): confirmed money is covered only for the listed perils, and theft
-- is not one of them, even a burglary that exclusion 1(c)(i) would allow.
`the safe` MEANS `a damaged` money `by` (LIST `directly` theft) `where` (LIST `stated as insured`)
`a burglary of the safe` MEANS
    `a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of` (LIST `the safe`) `with theft` (JUST (`The circumstances of a theft` WITH `in the insured building` IS TRUE, `with force or violence to break in or to get out` IS TRUE)) `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` `good conduct` `premium` `the premium paid on time`
#ASSERT `the effect of the exclusions on` `a burglary of the safe` `the safe` EQUALS `excluded by` (LIST "exclusion 6")

§§ `Finding 15: the write-back of exclusion 1(c) is harder to meet than that of 1(a)`

-- The same pair of direct causes, an excluded one and fire: under 1(a) the fire's part is
-- covered; under 1(c), whose write-back joins its limbs with "và" (src:59-63), nothing is.
#ASSERT `the effect of the exclusions on` (`a loss of the item` (`a damaged` `machinery and equipment` `by` (LIST `directly` `latent defect`, `directly` fire))) (`a damaged` `machinery and equipment` `by` (LIST `directly` `latent defect`, `directly` fire)) EQUALS `excluded except for the part arising from a cause not excluded` (LIST "exclusion 1(a)")
#ASSERT `the effect of the exclusions on` (`a loss of the item` (`a damaged` `machinery and equipment` `by` (LIST `directly` `mechanical or electrical breakdown or derangement of machinery or equipment`, `directly` fire))) (`a damaged` `machinery and equipment` `by` (LIST `directly` `mechanical or electrical breakdown or derangement of machinery or equipment`, `directly` fire)) EQUALS `excluded by` (LIST "exclusion 1(c)")

§§ `Finding 16: tanks and pipes are excluded property`

-- Exclusion 8(d) (src:156-159) names "bể chứa" and "đường ống" (reservoirs, pipelines; also tanks
-- and pipes), the apparatus whose bursting exclusion 6 writes back (src:138-139). Read as tanks
-- and pipes, damage to them by fire is excluded.
#ASSERT `the effect of the exclusions on` (`a loss of the item` (`a damaged` pipelines `by` (LIST `directly` fire))) (`a damaged` pipelines `by` (LIST `directly` fire)) EQUALS `excluded by` (LIST "exclusion 8")
#ASSERT `the effect of the exclusions on` (`a loss of the item` (`a damaged` reservoirs `by` (LIST `directly` fire))) (`a damaged` reservoirs `by` (LIST `directly` fire)) EQUALS `excluded by` (LIST "exclusion 8")

§§ `Finding 17: an innocent and unconnected misstatement takes the property out`

-- General Condition 2 (src:262-268) asks for no intent and no link to the cause of the loss.
`the building, a fact omitted` MEANS `A damaged item` WITH
    `the item insured`                  IS `the building`
    `kind`                              IS buildings
    `the chain of causation`            IS LIST (`directly` lightning)
    `circumstances`                     IS `the ordinary circumstances`
    `valuation`                         IS `the ordinary valuation`
    `what the Insured told the Insurer` IS `What the Insured told the Insurer about the item` WITH
        `false information about the property, the building, the business or the premises` IS FALSE
        `a misstatement of a material fact`                                     IS FALSE
        `an omission of a fact on which the Insurer assessed the risk`          IS TRUE
    `changes under General Condition 8` IS EMPTY
    `claimed as a cost of changing or adding to a computer system, programme, software or chip` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `the answer for the claim` `the Schedule` (`a loss of the item` `the building, a fact omitted`) EQUALS `nothing is payable because` (LIST "General Condition 2: the property is affected by an omission of a fact on which the Insurer assessed the risk", "the amount for the loss, after the conditions, the caps and the deductible, is nil")

§§ `Finding 18: the sum insured is used up by earlier losses, but average still counts it in full`

-- The proviso caps liability for the whole period (src:20-23) with no reinstatement of the sum
-- insured; General Condition 14 (src:412-416) still compares the value with the full sum insured.
-- 900,000,000 already paid on the building; a second fire of 500,000,000 on a building worth
-- 1,200,000,000: average gives 500,000,000 x 1,000/1,200 = 416,666,666.67, and only 100,000,000
-- is left to pay.
`a second fire` MEANS `A damaged item` WITH
    `the item insured`                  IS `a scheduled item` "factory building" `insured for` 1000000000 `with paid already` 900000000
    `kind`                              IS buildings
    `the chain of causation`            IS LIST (`directly` fire)
    `circumstances`                     IS `the ordinary circumstances`
    `valuation`                         IS `Damage of` 500000000 `to property worth` 1200000000
    `what the Insured told the Insurer` IS `nothing false was said`
    `changes under General Condition 8` IS EMPTY
    `claimed as a cost of changing or adding to a computer system, programme, software or chip` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `General Condition 14 applied to` `a second fire` 500000000 GREATER THAN 416666666
#ASSERT `the amount for the item` `a second fire` `given` `no exclusion applies` EQUALS 100000000

§§ `Finding 19: an "all risks" policy that excludes Damage from an unknown cause`

-- Exclusion 1(c)(iii) lists "không rõ nguyên nhân" (unknown cause) (src:51); the write-back needs
-- a cause not excluded, which an unknown cause cannot supply.
#ASSERT `the effect of the exclusions on` (`a loss of the item` (`a damaged` stock `by` (LIST `directly` `an unknown cause`))) (`a damaged` stock `by` (LIST `directly` `an unknown cause`)) EQUALS `excluded by` (LIST "exclusion 1(c)")
